WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.119 --> 00:00:12.659
While Mr.

2
00:00:12.699 --> 00:00:14.080
Havisham was visiting Mrs.

3
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.921
Errol, Cedric was visiting his best friend.

4
00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.442
Mr. Hobbs owned the corner grocery store.

5
00:00:22.842 --> 00:00:25.523
As Cedric sat in the store, he thought Mr.

6
00:00:25.543 --> 00:00:28.024
Hobbs must be rich to own such a place.

7
00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:34.251
It was filled with so many different kinds of food—from prunes to biscuits.

8
00:00:36.192 --> 00:00:39.874
Mr. Hobbs also owned a horse and wagon for making deliveries.

9
00:00:41.195 --> 00:00:41.835
As for Mr.

10
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:44.817
Hobbs himself, he was annoyed by most people.

11
00:00:46.257 --> 00:00:48.539
But he always enjoyed Cedric's company.

12
00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.482
That day he was reading aloud from the newspaper while Cedric perched on a stool.

13
00:00:54.502 --> 00:00:57.824
"Look at this picture from England!"

14
00:00:58.672 --> 00:01:03.696
Mr. Hobbs held up the paper so Cedric could see a ceremony at Queen Victoria's palace.

15
00:01:03.716 --> 00:01:08.679
"All those earls, sitting around doing nothing."

16
00:01:08.699 --> 00:01:12.481
"Have you known many earls, Mr.

17
00:01:12.521 --> 00:01:14.503
Hobbs?" Cedric asked.

18
00:01:14.523 --> 00:01:17.425
"I should say not!"

19
00:01:17.845 --> 00:01:19.866
Mr. Hobbs replied indignantly.

20
00:01:19.886 --> 00:01:22.208
"They're all tyrants.

21
00:01:22.888 --> 00:01:28.192
I won't have any of them sitting around here wearing their fancy velvet robes and coronets."

22
00:01:29.932 --> 00:01:31.673
"What's a coronet?"

23
00:01:32.253 --> 00:01:33.173
Cedric asked.

24
00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:36.495
"A little crown," Mr.

25
00:01:36.535 --> 00:01:38.135
Hobbs said with disgust.

26
00:01:39.636 --> 00:01:41.277
Cedric was familiar with Mr.

27
00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:43.378
Hobbs' poor opinion of the British.

28
00:01:44.998 --> 00:01:47.479
They had been the enemy during the American Revolution.

29
00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.140
He also knew that Mr.

30
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.041
Hobbs especially disliked the aristocracy.

31
00:01:53.061 --> 00:02:00.248
"Maybe earls wouldn't want to be earls if they knew it was a bad thing," Cedric said.

32
00:02:00.268 --> 00:02:03.390
"Ha! They love being earls!

33
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.471
Everybody else does all their work.

34
00:02:07.451 --> 00:02:08.772
Why would they give that up?"

35
00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:13.314
They were in the middle of this conversation when Mrs.

36
00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:15.355
Errol's servant, Mary, appeared.

37
00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:18.516
Her face was flushed with excitement.

38
00:02:18.536 --> 00:02:22.498
"Come home, darling," Mary said to Cedric.

39
00:02:23.518 --> 00:02:24.598
"Your mother needs you."

40
00:02:26.499 --> 00:02:27.960
Cedric slipped off the stool.

41
00:02:29.068 --> 00:02:30.929
"Does she want me to take a walk with her?"

42
00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:33.591
Mary shook her head.

43
00:02:34.611 --> 00:02:38.653
She had such an odd look on her face that Cedric immediately began to worry.

44
00:02:38.673 --> 00:02:41.355
"Is something wrong with Mama?"

45
00:02:41.795 --> 00:02:42.695
Cedric asked.

46
00:02:42.715 --> 00:02:45.657
"Has the hot sun given her a headache?"

47
00:02:47.078 --> 00:02:50.059
"No, but something unusual has happened.

48
00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.200
Come along now."

49
00:02:52.521 --> 00:02:54.922
Mary motioned for Cedric to accompany her.

50
00:02:56.983 --> 00:03:02.059
When Cedric reached home, he was puzzled to see a carriage waiting in front of his house.

51
00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:06.382
"Hurry upstairs and put on your best clothes!"

52
00:03:06.903 --> 00:03:07.603
Mary said.

53
00:03:08.844 --> 00:03:13.388
As Cedric passed the parlor door, he noticed his mother sitting on the sofa.

54
00:03:14.509 --> 00:03:18.512
She was talking to a stranger, who sat perfectly straight in his chair.

55
00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.155
The stranger looked very serious.

56
00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:25.978
Mrs. Errol heard his footsteps.

57
00:03:25.998 --> 00:03:29.721
"There's Cedric," she said to Mr.

58
00:03:29.741 --> 00:03:33.382
Havisham. "He's back from visiting his good friend Mr.

59
00:03:33.422 --> 00:03:35.984
Hobbs." "Who's Mr.

60
00:03:36.104 --> 00:03:39.825
Hobbs?" "The owner of the grocery store."

61
00:03:39.845 --> 00:03:43.107
"Of course," Mr.

62
00:03:43.147 --> 00:03:44.668
Havisham said quietly.

63
00:03:45.768 --> 00:03:48.589
Once again he wondered what kind of boy Cedric was.

64
00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:53.732
In his world, gentlemen's sons didn't make friends with grocers.

65
00:03:56.596 --> 00:04:00.678
When Cedric came downstairs, he was wearing a cream-colored suit.

66
00:04:01.639 --> 00:04:04.160
Mary had neatly combed his blond curls.

67
00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:07.582
"Oh, Cedric!"

68
00:04:08.603 --> 00:04:10.444
Mrs. Errol held out her arms.

69
00:04:11.924 --> 00:04:14.646
Cedric ran to his mother and gave her a hug.

70
00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:20.609
The tall stranger rose from his chair and studied Cedric from head to toe.

71
00:04:20.629 --> 00:04:25.512
"So this is Lord Fauntleroy!"

72
00:04:27.192 --> 00:04:29.433
"I'm sorry, sir, but you're mistaken.

73
00:04:30.614 --> 00:04:31.974
I'm Cedric Errol."

74
00:04:34.135 --> 00:04:36.656
Cedric went over and shook the man's hand.

75
00:04:37.916 --> 00:04:41.898
Mr. Havisham couldn't help smiling at this boy who acted like an adult.

76
00:04:41.918 --> 00:04:44.099
"I'm Mr.

77
00:04:44.139 --> 00:04:47.240
Havisham, the Earl of Dorincourt's lawyer."

78
00:04:48.681 --> 00:04:50.141
Cedric's eyes widened.

79
00:04:50.161 --> 00:04:53.523
"You know a real earl?

80
00:04:54.323 --> 00:04:55.504
Wait until I tell Mr.

81
00:04:55.564 --> 00:04:59.157
Hobbs. We were just talking about earls!"

82
00:04:59.177 --> 00:05:03.059
"Come sit next to me."

83
00:05:03.839 --> 00:05:05.620
Cedric's mother patted the sofa.

84
00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:10.042
"Mr. Havisham has some news for you."

85
00:05:11.442 --> 00:05:13.163
For the next hour, Mr.

86
00:05:13.183 --> 00:05:14.424
Havisham and Mrs.

87
00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:16.605
Errol went over the story with Cedric.

88
00:05:17.905 --> 00:05:23.488
He kept repeating, "You mean, I'll be a real earl someday?"

89
00:05:24.688 --> 00:05:28.849
As the two adults continued to talk, Cedric listened quietly.

90
00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:35.471
When Mary brought tea, Cedric passed the cookies to Mr.

91
00:05:35.491 --> 00:05:37.351
Havisham before taking one himself.

92
00:05:38.852 --> 00:05:41.333
Mr. Havisham was impressed with his good manners.

93
00:05:41.353 --> 00:05:47.714
"What a charming, friendly child he is," Mr.

94
00:05:47.754 --> 00:05:48.674
Havisham thought.

95
00:05:48.694 --> 00:05:55.933
"I'm still not sure I understand all this," Cedric said as Mr.

96
00:05:55.973 --> 00:05:57.374
Havisham stood up to leave.

97
00:05:57.394 --> 00:06:01.437
"You will understand in time," Mr.

98
00:06:01.477 --> 00:06:02.357
Havisham said.

99
00:06:02.378 --> 00:06:07.041
"I think you'll find it's quite nice to be an earl.

100
00:06:08.061 --> 00:06:10.763
You'll be extremely wealthy one day."

101
00:06:13.405 --> 00:06:17.408
After the front door closed, Cedric gave his mother a mournful look.

102
00:06:17.428 --> 00:06:20.270
"I don't want to leave New York.

103
00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.412
There has to be a way out of this, Mama!"

104
00:06:25.988 --> 00:06:28.209
"I'm sorry, Cedric," Mrs.

105
00:06:28.369 --> 00:06:29.029
Errol said.

106
00:06:29.049 --> 00:06:32.830
"Your grandfather has sent for you, and you must go.

107
00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:36.071
I believe it's what your father would have wanted.

108
00:06:36.091 --> 00:06:40.693
The news is a shock to me, too, but at least I'll be coming with you."

109
00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:43.634
Cedric hung his head.

110
00:06:43.654 --> 00:06:46.295
"None of my friends are earls.

111
00:06:47.315 --> 00:06:49.476
I don't know why I have to be one."
